# The published tree: every archive built from this repository (an archive of
# a release commit, and a forge's source tarball for a tag) leaves these out.
#
# The agent files (CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, .claude/, .serena/) and every
# workflow under .github/workflows except the two below are published, and
# scanned like any other file: they carry no internal host, repository or
# domain (owner ruling on #406 and #407, option (a)). test/releasability
# enforces this list and scans everything it leaves in
# (docs/release/public-releasability.md).
#
# The private forge's own workflows stay out. They are not the CI template:
# they drive only the private forge's SDLC -- arming its auto-merge
# (automerge), opening its revert PR when a merge turns main red
# (revert-red-main) and running its pull-request review on its own runners
# (code-review, the company template verbatim) -- and nothing a public reader
# runs calls or reads them.
.github/workflows/automerge.yml export-ignore
.github/workflows/revert-red-main.yml export-ignore
.github/workflows/code-review.yml export-ignore

# The private repository's release trust anchor stays out: it pins the
# internal principal `make release-alpha` verifies against by default, and a
# public maintainer names their own signers file with RELEASE_ALLOWED_SIGNERS.
/.release-allowed-signers export-ignore
